    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "core.input.comment",
      "name": "comment",
      "x": 62.9,
      "y": 9.1,
      "text": "The sampleScrubber uses a sample as a waveshaping function. You can connect an oscillator to the \"in\" port to drive the waveshaper.\n\nTo Do:\n* Click the \"record\" button on the \"recorder\" and record a few seconds of your voice using a microphone.\n* Click the \"play\" or \"pause\" button to stop recording.\n* Click the \"learn\" button on the \"matchControl\" then move a MIDI controller, for example the mod wheel. Or just use the knob. The controls the frequency of the scanning oscillator.\n* Click on the xyPad and drag the blue dot around. The x axis is position in the sample. The y axis is the width of the scrubbing window. The on and off jacks are used to trigger an envelope.",
      "w": 792.875,
      "h": 239
    },
